{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he grew up.</b> And he is the servant of HaShem from Israel, or all of Israel:" "<b>[before Him].</b> Before the blessed Name:" "<b>[grew up] like a tender plant.</b> Like \"his shoots shall go forth\" (Hosea 14:7):" "<b>and like a root out of dry ground.</b> That it gives no fruit, that it does not grow:" "<b>no form to him.</b> Its meaning is like \"his form, from that of men\" (Isaiah 52:14):" "<b>and we saw him, and no appearance.</b> And not his own appearance, and furthermore with him, and likewise \"and no beauty that we should desire him,\" and like it \"a gift in secret covers up wrath\" (Proverbs 21:14):"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {5 "The phrase 'ואחר עמו' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:17.063223100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}